\section{Related work}
\label{sec:related}

\paragraph{Prediction-powered inference.}
PPI builds a valid interval for a mean, quantile or regression coefficient from a few gold-standard labels, many unlabeled records and a black-box predictor \citep{angelopoulos2023ppi}; PPI++ tunes a scalar weight $\lambda$ on the predictor and is the strongest published interval for the fixed-predictor setting we study \citep{angelopoulos2023ppipp}. Stratified PPI \citep{fisch2024stratified} recalibrates the predictor on strata, which is the closest published relative of using labels to build the control variate. Cro
